# The values this panel is built with. Committed on purpose — see .gitignore.
#
# Read at build time: Vite substitutes them into the bundle, so changing one
# means a rebuild, not a restart. A build argument of the same name overrides
# what is here, which is the escape hatch for a one-off build.

# Where the panel finds the API.
#
# The /api suffix is part of it: the API mounts its routes at /api
# (iigl-node/src/app.ts), so the base has to include it.
#
# A different origin from the panel, so the API must list this panel's origins in
# CORS_ORIGINS. Without it the preflight comes back with no
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin, the browser blocks every response, and the panel
# reports that it cannot reach the API at all.
#
# Origins, plural: the three sign-in doors are one build behind three domains,
# and CORS is matched on the exact Origin string, so all three have to be listed
# or two of the doors fail while the third works.
#
#   CORS_ORIGINS=https://admin.test.iigl.org,https://super.test.iigl.org,https://team.test.iigl.org
#
# SESSION_CROSS_SITE is **not** needed for this pairing, and should stay off.
# The session cookie is SameSite=Lax, and SameSite is judged on the registrable
# domain rather than the origin: admin.test.iigl.org and api.iigl.org are both
# iigl.org, so these requests are same-site and the cookie is sent normally.
# Lax is also this API's only CSRF defence — there is no token — so giving it up
# buys nothing here. It would only be required if the panel moved to a
# different registrable domain.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.iigl.org/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploads. Pictures are shrunk in the browser before they are sent; all four are
# clamped in src/lib/image.ts, so a typo falls back to the default rather than
# ruining a week of scans. Commented out means the default applies.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# JPEG/WebP quality, 0.4-1.
# VITE_IMAGE_QUALITY=0.82

# Longest edge in pixels, 600-6000.
# VITE_IMAGE_MAX_EDGE=2000

# Leave anything smaller than this alone, in KB, 0-5000.
# VITE_IMAGE_SKIP_UNDER_KB=300

# Largest picture somebody may choose, in MB, 8-128 — before shrinking.
# VITE_UPLOAD_MAX_MB=32
